SM(479,{"n":"Acts 20 Conclusion","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Acts 20 Conclusion.mp3","d":2651.6,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest, serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.52,"But we, notice again, it's we, because St."],[24.72,"Luke is there too."],[27.68,"But we sailed away from Philippi after the days of unleavened bread, and in five days joined them at Troaz, where we stayed seven days."],[41.36,"So because they went up north, they're now sort of going around and then down to Antioch."],[48.0,"So it's a sort of longer, more circuitous route."],[53.96,"Given the region they're in, is that the same as Troy?"],[58.4,"Uh no. Okay."],[59.84,"Uh huh No."],[61.64,"They might have claimed to be at some point."],[64.6,"There was a Roman Troy that is not in the same spot as the actual Troy of the Trojan the Trojan War."],[74.68,"There were several places that claimed to be, because already at this point they'd lost track of where exactly it was."],[83.48,"But on the first day of the week, when the disciples came together to break bread, we'll pause there for a second."],[94.78,"Because I've been saying this the whole time, and you've been believing me because you're kind and good people."],[100.94,"But now it's here in black and white."],[104.08,"Remember, I've been saying that we we've had them going to the synagogues."],[107.33,"We've seen the Christians still going to the synagogues, but they're preaching Christ and learning about Christ in the synagogue."],[112.47,"On the Sabbath, seventh day of the week."],[115.29,"Here we have explicitly, on the first day of the week."],[118.85,"The Christians are gathering just the Christians."],[122.3,"And the on Sunday, first day of the week."],[124.48,"And the reason they're doing that is to break bread."],[127.04,"That's when they're celebrating the Eucharist."],[129.76,"So it's different than what they do on Satan deal with the at the Sydney Con.versation"],[134.31,"And so this again is where we get the two pieces of our liturgy."],[137.85,"The first part of the liturgy."],[139.7,"We sing Psalms, then we read scripture, then we preach."],[144.34,"Which is what they did in the synagogue on the Sabbath"],[148.52,"Second part of the liturgy."],[150.46,"We celebrate the Eucharist."],[151.9,"That's what they did on Sunday."],[154.3,"And then in the second century, when the Christians were thrown out of the synagogue, they took that synagogue part and moved that to Sunday also."],[163.02,"Okay. So that the whole thing would be on Sunday as a Christian gathering."],[173.02,"Paul, ready to depart the next day, spoke to them and continued his message until midnight."],[179.86,"I don't think I could get away with going a half hour without people either doing this."],[187.82,"Or getting up and walking out, or falling asleep, rolling their eyes a lot."],[195.78,"But he kept going till midnight."],[198.8,"He kept preaching till midnight."],[202.0,"And we're told because he's about to leave."],[204.66,"So he says, okay, whatever I've got to say, I need to say it now, so he keeps going."],[210.34,"You gave him like three months' worth of huge scrolls for eat.hered together"],[223.34,"And in a window sat a certain young man named Eudicus who was sinking into a deep sleep."],[230.54,"Okay. So they were still human then."],[232.27,"And we're also told that this is a young man"],[233.51,"Uh-huh. The young man, Neoniscos, that means, you know, probably very young."],[242.33,"Uh-huh. I mean, we're talking a teenager, yeah, you know, teenager, probably."],[247.29,"Um, and so he's starting to doze off."],[251.77,"And he's sitting right in the window."],[254.49,"Now we think of windows, of course, as as having glass."],[259.29,"No glass. So this is a hole in the wall."],[262.41,"And remember, they're in in upper rooms, they're on the second floor."],[265.29,"Which is a wind hole."],[266.89,"Yes. So he's kind of sitting in the frame."],[270.99,"Probably wanted some fresh air or whatever."],[273.31,"And he's starting to doze off."],[274.91,"So it says where it says there were many lamps in the upper room where they gathered together"],[276.47,"Yeah. So what I was talking about before, what we do now is something that they didn't."],[286.07,"So when we light the candles, doesn't that symbolize us bringing our lamps to the is that what that's about, too?"],[294.55,"It's yeah, it's it's related to that."],[296.39,"They were already they're already burning lamps, and also um we know, and this is explicit in the book of Revelation when we get there, that churches gathering Christian gathering places for for Sundays for the first day of the week, had lamp stands, seven branch lampstands, like the one in the temple."],[318.79,"Okay. This is another connection between the the temple worship and the altar."],[321.03,"the That's what the thing on force."],[324.35,"And what we do now."],[330.11,"There's a seven-branch candlest."],[332.43,"Okay, so that's what that is."],[333.47,"See, that's why I'd ask that before, because I wanted to know more in detail about what we do today is."],[337.79,"There was one in the tabernacle, there's one in the temple, and there's one in our altar."],[342.99,"And that was already being that was already being done then."],[345.63,"Okay. Alright. Okay."],[347.15,"So now I'm going to go."],[351.08,"Okay. So Eutychus was overcome by sleep."],[356.52,"And as Paul continued speaking, he fell down from the third story and was taken up dead."],[362.84,"Okay, so he passes out, goes out the window."],[365.72,"He's on the third story, so he probably falls about 25 feet"],[370.86,"Lands of the road, he's dead."],[374.3,"But Paul went down, fell on him, and embracing him said, Do not trouble yourselves, for his life is in him."],[383.66,"So he says, Don't panic."],[389.34,"And when he had come up and broken bread and eaten and talked for a long while, even till daybreak, he departed."],[396.46,"And they brought the young man in alive, and they were not a little comforted."],[401.98,"There's another underplayed quasi-British translation."],[408.23,"And St So they they bring him up and he eats so they know he's alive."],[415.87,"Paul goes ahead and goes."],[418.99,"So St. Paul raised him from the dead."],[420.99,"This is one of the reasons why St."],[422.51,"Luke gives us the list of the people who were there."],[427.23,"Yeah. Witnessing a miracle."],[428.81,"From different cities."],[429.95,"Who could say, oh yeah, yeah, I remember when that happened."],[435.87,"And notice he he breaks the the breaking, actual breaking of the bread happens after the sermon."],[442.75,"So they could uh they couldn't do what some folks do now and go receive the Eucharist and bail out of church to listen to the uh to the whole sermon all the way past midnight."],[461.11,"Then we notice again it's we St."],[463.75,"Luke is still there."],[465.19,"Then we went ahead to the ship and sailed to Osos."],[469.67,"They're intending to take Paul on board, for so he had given orders, intending himself to go on foot."],[478.07,"So he was going to do uh he did part of the journey on foot."],[484.25,"Remember, you're sailing down the coast."],[486.7,"So he says, you know what?"],[488.38,"I'm gonna go ahead and do part of this overland down the road."],[491.84,"Because the Roman road also ran down the coast."],[497.48,"And when he met at us at Assos, we took him on board and came to Middle Anae."],[504.2,"We sailed from there, and the next day came opposite Chios."],[508.12,"So this is our travel log of the coast of Asia Minor in the Roman period."],[514.04,"The following day we arrived at Samos and stayed at Tregalium."],[518.52,"The next day we came to Miletus, for Paula decided to sail past Ephesus so that he would not have to spend time in Asia, for he was hurrying to be at Jerusalem, if possible, on the day of Pentecost."],[531.12,"So this should give us an idea of how long this third journey has been."],[538.34,"We've had little bits and pieces."],[540.52,"We had a year and a half at Ephesus and everything."],[542.88,"So this is going to be over two years by the time it's done."],[546.56,"Because remember the last time he was trying to get back to Jerusalem for Passover."],[551.92,"So you have a year and a half, plus now he's trying to get to Pentecost, which is 50 days, like two months after the Passover."],[559.44,"So he's got it's been a full two years plus a little bit."],[564.24,"And so he says, you know what?"],[565.92,"Let's not stop at Ephesus."],[567.76,"Let's just keep going because I want to try and make it to Jerusalem by Pentecost."],[572.16,"That's the plan, at least."],[575.2,"From Miletus, he sent to Ephesus and called for the elders of the church."],[580.16,"When they had come to the and so he sends word down to them while they're at Miletus."],[585.6,"I don't want to stop at Ephesus, but I do want to see them."],[586.16,"at Ephesus. The Presbyters, who he's appointed to lead the church"],[593.62,"So he says, Come, come up and uh visit with me."],[597.46,"So they make their way up to Miletus."],[601.14,"When they had come to them, to him, he said to them, You know from the first day that I came to Asia, in what manner I always lived among you, serving the Lord with all humility, with many tears and trials, which happened to me by the plotting of the Jews."],[617.14,"How I kept back nothing that was helpful, and proclaimed it to you and taught you publicly, and from house to house, testifying to Jews and also to Greeks, repentance toward God and faith toward our Lord Jesus Christ."],[632.06,"So he says, you know, you saw what I did and how I did it."],[636.71,"Remember, these are the presbyters, so these are the people who are the leaders in that church."],[642.73,"So he's kind of telling telling them this is now what you need to continue to do when I'm not there."],[650.27,"He says, I went house to house."],[652.56,"I didn't hold anything back."],[654.66,"Everything I had to say, I said."],[656.83,"I taught everyone for free."],[659.31,"We need need we to keep keep that in account."],[663.09,"Because that was not the normal in the ancient world."],[665.79,"Anymore than it's normal in our time."],[667.49,"You want to take a class, you have to pay tuition."],[671.19,"Well, at that time, people didn't. take disciples on for free"],[675.12,"People, if you were going to go and study with a philosopher or, you know, anyone."],[680.53,"You were going to uh you were gonna pay them either directly or if you were going to study like with a craftsman as like a journeyman, you were gonna be paying with your labor."],[692.31,"You were gonna be doing all the grunt work and jobs he didn't want to do while he taught you how to be a smith or uh you know a wagon ride or whatever it was you were learning to do."],[702.49,"And so that's that's what St."],[703.77,"Paul is getting at when he says, You saw how I held nothing back, and I to I didn't say, you know, if you want to learn more, you know, buy my book for 1999."],[712.38,"Is this also uh beginning to talk against the idea of secret doctrines that uh yeah are k are kept back from most of the things."],[723.62,"That's that's the publicly part."],[725.38,"Uh-huh. Yeah. That's the publicly."],[727.94,"Said it all publicly out in the open."],[730.9,"I didn't hold anything back."],[732.19,"Proclaim it to everybody that that's what you need to do too."],[735.07,"You need to proclaim everything publicly."],[737.39,"You need to not be looking to take money."],[740.17,"Get rich off of this, you know, off of you know the kingdom you, need to just proclaim and teach everything all the time, every chance you get."],[749.01,"Go to people's houses and talk to 'em."],[751.26,"Preach it at first day of the week at the gathering, preach it in the synagogue, preach it on the street like St."],[756.22,"Paul did in the marketplaces."],[757.58,"Proclaim it to everyone"],[762.34,"Again, he points out not just to Jewish people, but to everybody."],[768.1,"And then he preached repentance toward God and faith toward our Lord Jesus Christ."],[777.7,"Some people will look at this and try and say, oh, see, St."],[781.06,"Paul doesn't believe in the Trinity because they're too separate."],[785.94,"He says, God and Jesus."],[789.34,"Here's why that's not true."],[793.42,"It's not true because he calls him, he calls him our Lord Jesus Christ."],[802.06,"Kyrios is one of the other titles for the God of Israel."],[808.54,"The fundamental quote unquote creed of believing Jewish people to this day, true then, but to this day, is from Deuteronomy."],[819.1,"It's called the Shema."],[820.38,"It's here, O Israel, the Lord your God, the Lord is one God."],[829.02,"You notice there, Lord and God are one."],[835.34,"So when St."],[836.54,"Paul says God and our Lord Jesus Christ."],[842.08,"He's saying that God the Father and Jesus Christ are one."],[845.64,"So he's actually making a a tr Trininitaritariany, or at least a binatarian, but statement here, not the opposite"],[852.96,"And we're going to see in his epistles, there are there's one place in particular in First Corinthians where he literally takes the words of the Shema in Greek and inserts the name Jesus and the Father to make it abundantly clear that what he's saying is that the one God of Israel is three persons."],[875.68,"And anyone anyone, even somewhat in the religion, even as an outsider, would probably catch it."],[882.4,"Would pick up on that instant on that instant."],[884.4,"Because they uh they they would have heard it at a synagogue every single meeting."],[890.64,"Prayed and so they used they used the Shema at this time in history Pharisees in particular used the Shema the way Orthodox folks pray the Jesus prayer."],[902.52,"Uh-huh. Oh they would just recite it again and again and again."],[908.2,"Okay. So yeah they you'd take those words and add other ones they'd notice they'd know exactly what you were doing."],[920.17,"Yeah. Instantly but the two things notice it's repentance and faith."],[929.69,"And we've talked about how, but it's been a while, because I think the last time we talked about this may have been back in John 1."],[936.25,"So I'll comment on it at least briefly here again"],[939.97,"Faith is not passing a true-false test."],[946.57,"We talk about faith and belief as if, you know, there's one God."],[952.33,"True. That one God is three persons."],[956.49,"True. Jesus died for my sin."],[959.47,"True. And if you mark all the true, get all the true-false uh answers"],[964.45,"then you have faith. Um"],[967.17,"Because we're thinking about faith as opposed to like modern atheists."],[972.79,"Who would say, no, there is no God."],[975.24,"Um that's not what faith is, biblically."],[978.76,"Uh St When the New Testament talks about faith, that's not what they're talking about."],[983.6,"James is gonna make this abundantly clear in his epistles because he's gonna point out that every demon in hell would get the true-false test right."],[991.92,"Satan himself knows there's only one God."],[996.17,"knows that that one God is three persons because he's met them."],[1000.7,"And all those things he knows that Jesus died for the sins of the world."],[1004.75,"He doesn't just believe it, he knows it."],[1007.2,"And that's not doing him any good."],[1008.8,"We wouldn't say he has faith."],[1010.94,"So contained within the word that we translate as faith is the is the idea of faithfulness."],[1018.31,"Meaning of loyalty."],[1021.21,"Of allegiance. There were no atheists at the time the New Testament was written."],[1026.59,"There was nobody walking around who thought there were no gods at all."],[1032.99,"So it's not which God."],[1035.73,"If you say faith in Jesus Christ, having faith in Jesus Christ, that doesn't just mean, oh yeah, I believe there was a Jesus Christ."],[1044.27,"That means you are loyal to him, your allegiance is to him, you serve him as opposed to these other gods, these other lords, these other masters."],[1055.01,"You stay loyal to him, you worship him as opposed to all of these other he's the one who you give worship and glory to."],[1059.17,"of That's what the idea faith in the New Testament is."],[1067.37,"Okay. So, and that's going to be important because the next book we're going to get into is going to be Romans."],[1076.25,"And when St."],[1077.29,"Paul says you're saved by faith, if you're thinking that means by getting the answers right on the truefalse test, you're not going to understand what St."],[1088.01,"Paul is saying."],[1091.53,"And you're going to become a Lutheran."],[1096.73,"No, no, I'm not kidding about that."],[1098.73,"But there's going to be you're going to have the problem that St."],[1102.57,"James is going to point to in his epistle, where you're going to say, Oh, well, you're just saved by believing those things."],[1107.65,"It doesn't matter what you do."],[1111.75,"Whereas if you understand what St."],[1113.67,"Paul means by faith, you understand that having faith then means doing a whole bunch of things."],[1119.75,"And not doing a whole bunch of other things."],[1123.31,"So, but we'll get into that more then."],[1125.23,"But it's important because that's how St."],[1127.07,"Paul is using it here, too."],[1129.73,"He's not just saying, okay, come and repent of your sins once and then profess that Jesus is the Messiah once, and boom, now you're saved."],[1138.87,"You're good. You're a Christian now."],[1141.21,"That this is an ongoing thing."],[1143.91,"Because he's telling them they have to continue to preach it."],[1145.11,"to continue to preach. You need to continue to preach repentance towards God, and you need faith in Jesus Christ"],[1153.31,"Because people, the people need to continue in both of those things."],[1158.59,"And see, now I go bound in the Spirit to Jerusalem, not knowing the things that will happen to me there, except that the Holy Spirit testifies in every city, saying that chains and tribulations await me."],[1173.31,"So St. Paul has the firm impression that some bad stuff is going to go down when he gets to Jerusalem."],[1182.19,"He has good reason to just to believe that in general, beyond the fact that the Holy Spirit is communicating this to him, that he needs to be prepared for this."],[1190.03,"We remember the things that had been going on in Jerusalem the last time we were there in Acts, which was a lot of persecution."],[1190.91,"Of the church, St"],[1197.56,"Peter being thrown in prison, St."],[1199.16,"James the son of Zebedee being killed."],[1201.46,"St. Stephen was killed."],[1203.14,"So things have not been good in Jerusalem in general."],[1206.34,"He's had a lot of run-ins on the way with members of the synagogue community."],[1211.86,"He's fairly certain word of that has gotten back to the Jewish leaders in Jerusalem."],[1217.14,"So he's he's anticipating that this is not going to go well."],[1221.14,"He may end up being killed there."],[1225.5,"And so that's why it is so important to him now to give this charge to the leadership of the Church of Ephesus so that they'll be able to continue in case they never see him again in the body."],[1240.06,"But none of these things move me, nor do I count my life dear to myself, so that I may finish my race with joy, and the ministry which I receive from the Lord Jesus to testify to the gospel of the grace of God."],[1254.14,"So he says, but"],[1256.44,"He's not saying, oh, this bad stuff's awaiting me in Jerusalem, so maybe I won't go there."],[1261.69,"He says, I'm I'm still going there."],[1264.11,"And he he says, I'm not worried about trying to save my own life."],[1268.12,"If this is the time when I'm going to die, then so be it."],[1273.02,"I need to see this through."],[1274.58,"Now, is the reason he's so determined to go to Jerusalem to be there for the feast?"],[1280.9,"Is that the motivation?"],[1283.22,"Well, he's he's got several things going on."],[1285.94,"Um one of them, as has been mentioned a few times in Acts, is that he's been taking up a collection uh from the the new churches and the Gentile churches for the Christians in Jerusalem who are in crushing poverty."],[1301.54,"Because most of the peasants in Judea are in crushing poverty."],[1304.82,"They're not Roman citizens, but especially the Christians now, because they've sort of become pariahs in the Jewish community on top of everything else."],[1312.5,"So the other peasants don't even like them."],[1315.62,"So he's taking up this collection, he needs to deliver that collection."],[1320.52,"He needs to go there for the feast."],[1323.52,"He believes that this is where he needs to go as much as he knows that this is not going to be pleasant."],[1333.33,"And indeed, now I know that you all you all, among whom I have gone preaching the kingdom of God, will see my face no more."],[1342.95,"So he says, I'm pretty convinced you're not going to see me again in the body."],[1349.2,"And he spent a significant spent a year and a half, remember, in Ephesus, preaching and appointing these presbyters and working with them."],[1356.32,"Therefore, I testify to you this day that I am innocent of the blood of all men."],[1362.56,"Now, this is interesting."],[1365.48,"Because is he?"],[1366.92,"Who thought he wasn't?"],[1368.84,"Somebody who read the first few chapters of the book of Acts."],[1373.0,"Oh, well, you know, when you when he was persecuting Christians."],[1376.76,"Yeah. Oh, oh, yeah."],[1379.48,"Like St. Stephen and the other Christians."],[1383.72,"So this is an interesting statement."],[1386.22,"He's going to expand on it."],[1387.42,"But I'm just pausing here to note."],[1389.18,"Uh huh. To note here."],[1393.76,"For I am not shunned to declare to you the whole counsel of God."],[1399.6,"Well, we'll pause there again."],[1401.6,"Why is he innocent of every man's blood?"],[1405.04,"Because of what he's preached."],[1407.12,"Okay. So that's not why he's innocent of the blood before he was a Christian."],[1413.9,"He was baptized."],[1415.92,"He repented. This is a parallel to a very interesting passage in the book of 1 Kings."],[1427.36,"When Solomon has royally messed up."],[1431.2,"When we loop all the way back around there, that'll be a while."],[1433.92,"But we get all the error to Solomon."],[1436.32,"So we have Solomon in our heads as being this sort of great and wonderful king."],[1439.92,"He was actually really wicked."],[1441.76,"And we'll see that."],[1444.88,"That's why he loses the kingdom."],[1447.12,"That's why the kingdom's divided, and his son only gets a tiny part of it."],[1451.76,"But when that happens, his son gets two tribes."],[1453.45,"son. The other ten tribes go to Jeroboam the of Nebat"],[1458.69,"And God comes to Jeroboam, says a prophet, but to Jeroboam son of Nebat, and he says to him, he says, If you uh he says, I will give make your throne eternal."],[1470.53,"A descendant of yours will always sit on the throne of Israel, just like the promise I made to David."],[1476.85,"If you walk in all of my ways and keep all of my laws, the way David did."],[1483.33,"Okay. Now, he, of course, does not even come close."],[1487.99,"But what's interesting is that, like David did."],[1492.79,"Aside from the adultery, the murderer."],[1497.13,"Yeah. But what this shows us is repentance is actually real."],[1507.15,"When St. Paul repented and was baptized, he's not a murderer anymore."],[1514.36,"He's going to be honest about it in the epistles."],[1517.24,"He's going to say, I was a murderer."],[1520.6,"But it was."],[1522.45,"It's past tense."],[1523.57,"He's not one anymore."],[1525.17,"And there's going to be a very important passage in 1 Corinthians that we're going to get to."],[1529.33,"Where he lists a whole bunch of sins."],[1532.69,"He lists a whole bunch of sins."],[1535.25,"He talks about, you know, theft and drunkenness and homosexuality and adultery and all kinds of things."],[1540.37,"Gives us a big list, and he says, and such were some of you"],[1547.77,"Past tense. The people of the church in Corinth."],[1553.93,"You know? A lot of you were those things."],[1558.65,"He says, but you were washed with the blood of Christ."],[1563.77,"That's done. So this isn't just imagery or a talking point for St."],[1569.61,"Paul or for the scriptures."],[1571.69,"That when someone is baptized, they die and they rise again to a new life."],[1578.73,"And that when we come and we repent."],[1581.03,"The fathers talk about how the tears of repentance are like a second baptism."],[1584.59,"When we've sinned and we repent, you know, the tears of repentance wash us clean again"],[1592.21,"And that that's a reality."],[1595.81,"That's a reality."],[1596.93,"It's done. We are a different person after that than we were."],[1601.97,"So St. Paul, when he says, I mean, this is the blood of all men, isn't talking about that stuff before."],[1606.93,"His baptism has already taken care of that."],[1609.73,"That life is over and done with."],[1614.81,"Reason he says now he's innocent of all men to them is because of what he said before."],[1620.57,"That he's preached everything publicly in the open to everyone."],[1627.93,"But what does that mean?"],[1629.05,"What does the reverse of that mean?"],[1633.05,"That means if we see someone in sin, if we see someone perishing, if we see someone who needs to hear about the love of Christ, and we don't tell them, and we don't preach it to them, we don't proclaim it to them, we don't try and help them, we don't care."],[1654.06,"Then we're guilty, we're an accessory in modern legal terms to what they're doing if we say nothing."],[1662.22,"Yeah. I just I have a couple quick questions"],[1665.02,"One of my neighbors, there's a couple of my neighbors next door."],[1667.5,"You know what they for the way I' fimxing to tal aboutk in a rough neighborhood, but it's really not that bad."],[1671.26,"They're drug heads, big time."],[1673.18,"I mean, not just a little like a whole lot."],[1673.9,"And I bought one of them, it was a St"],[1677.54,"Michael candle, and I told him I said I'll s but Stephan is his first name."],[1682.34,"I said, Stephan, look, I bought this for you."],[1684.5,"And I and um and I said, you know, I I'll say prayers for you because he is really out there and I'm scared for him."],[1692.18,"I mean, I tried."],[1693.94,"And I tried to reach him, but I'm scared of those people too."],[1696.58,"At the same time, there's a couple of them and they're v violent and they're not nice people."],[1700.9,"I mean, I'm scared to I don't think they would kill me, but I'm saying but what you've just told me is that you didn't talk to her, reach out to him and say that you're gonna pray for them."],[1710.58,"That's not refusing to say anything."],[1712.42,"Yeah. Okay, so I'm going to that say's the same."],[1714.26,"But he's he's talking to the press he's talking to these presbyters."],[1717.86,"Yeah. And s who are gonna be leaders in the church"],[1721.73,"He's saying you can't just shrink away from this stuff."],[1726.04,"You can't get scared of the people in the church."],[1729.4,"You know, if you've got someone at your door who's living this life in sin, you can't just, you know, well, I don't I don't know, I don't want to make waves, or he gives a lot of money, or"],[1741.01,"That that that makes you an accessory."],[1743.99,"Now you can't force anyone to do anything, you can't right."],[1747.75,"But there's a difference between that and withholding what you know to be true."],[1752.4,"And what you know they need to hear."],[1755.3,"But chickening out of saying it."],[1758.92,"Because there comes a point where that person, if they continue down that road, especially, will end up destroying themselves"],[1764.72,"And then it's going to be too late for you to come back and say something or do something."],[1771.5,"So St. Paul is saying, look, I'm innocent of that, because I've laid it all out there publicly all the time."],[1779.0,"And you need to do the same."],[1783.48,"This is also where I stole the title of my podcast, my blog."],[1788.36,"That reference to the Whole Counsel of God."],[1793.4,"Therefore, take heed to yourselves and to all the flock among which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers to shepherd the church of God which he purchased with his own blood."],[1805.52,"This is another important verse, because notice what he just said."],[1809.36,"The church that God purchased with his own blood."],[1823.28,"Well, St. Paul just said it."],[1825.13,"This is the doctrine of the incarnation right here."],[1828.41,"God has blood."],[1830.17,"Because Jesus Christ is God and He has blood."],[1837.29,"And so he says, this is this is then what you need to do because of what I just said."],[1843.43,"Take heed to yourselves, not just to the flock."],[1848.6,"To yourselves to make sure your own life is in order, and then to those whom God has put you in authority over."],[1855.58,"Because this isn't just to presbyters, this isn't just to priests."],[1858.88,"This is to all of us."],[1860.44,"We take heed to ourselves, and then there are in various situations people who we're in a position of authority over, and we're responsible for them too."],[1868.78,"And what he's saying is those people who you're in authority over, wherever it is, if you're their boss, if you're their parent."],[1875.44,"If you're their aunt or uncle or grandparent or whatever."],[1878.33,"These are people who are so precious to God, each one of them, that he died for them."],[1884.51,"He purchased them at a very high price."],[1886.75,"That's how much he cares about them."],[1887.95,"them. And you need to keep that in mind when you're interacting with them and when you're caring for"],[1894.47,"Remember who they are."],[1897.59,"And that will inform how you treat them and how you care for them and how you try to guide them and lead them."],[1914.87,"There are going to be people who come."],[1918.07,"For the people in the church, and also for whoever it is, who you may have under your authority."],[1924.48,"There are going to be people who are going to come and try to lead them off."],[1928.16,"Try and harm them."],[1929.58,"Try and hurt them."],[1931.58,"Also from among yourselves, men will rise up, speaking perverse things to draw away the disciples after themselves."],[1939.44,"So it's not just outsiders coming and attacking."],[1942.32,"But there's going to be people who are part of your family or part of your community or part who are gonna become like those wolves too."],[1950.64,"And turn on each other."],[1953.28,"Therefore, watch and remember that for three years I did not cease to warn everyone night and day with tears."],[1968.88,"To never cease in treating with constant tears."],[1973.84,"Paul was I'm not there yet."],[1975.56,"I'm nowhere near as good a uh pastor as St."],[1979.96,"I'm working on it."],[1981.82,"But that shows you, St."],[1984.38,"Paul's heart, that this wasn't just, well, this is my job."],[1987.95,"This is my duty, this is my responsibility, so I guess."],[1992.27,"But he passionately cares about each one of them and about what happens to them."],[1996.83,"And when he sees them going astray, when he sees them going the wrong way, his response is what?"],[2002.75,"Not anger. Not to cut them off or throw them out, excommunicate them."],[2007.74,"His response is tears."],[2010.38,"He treats what happens to them as if it happened to himself."],[2017.66,"So now, brethren, I commend you to God and to the word of his grace, which is able to build you up and give you an inheritance among all those who are sanctified."],[2028.58,"So he says, I'm gonna be gone."],[2032.1,"I'm not gonna be able to give you any more of these sermons."],[2036.1,"So I commend you."],[2038.9,"I commend you to continue to be built up."],[2041.46,"In this case, the word of his grace actually does mean the scriptures."],[2045.78,"At this point, if you continue in that, that builds you up means you'll continue to learn to grow."],[2060.78,"There's leaders, and that'll lead you to what is the goal?"],[2063.94,"An inheritance. inheritance We think of as, oh hey, somebody left me something nice in their will."],[2066.06,"Remember the word inheritance."],[2071.04,"Inheritance in this context, in the context of the Old Testament, the inheritance was the promised land."],[2080.06,"That was the inheritance."],[2081.98,"Your tribe, your family, your people had an inheritance within the promised land."],[2087.18,"So he's talking about the world to come."],[2088.86,"He's talking about glory with God."],[2095.26,"I have coveted no one's silver or gold or apparel."],[2100.46,"Yes, you yourselves know that these hands have provided for my necessities and for those who are with me."],[2107.26,"I have shown you in every way by laboring like this that you must support the weak."],[2112.26,"And remember the words of the Lord Jesus that he said, it is more blessed to give than to receive."],[2118.34,"So he says, Saw, I didn't show up here, you know, trying to extract money from you."],[2124.02,"Right again, there was no buy my book."],[2127.3,"There was no, you know, buy me a house."],[2130.32,"There was no."],[2131.29,"I wasn't here to make money."],[2133.21,"And again, he's saying to them, that means you're not here to try and enrich yourselves."],[2139.29,"You worked as a tent maker."],[2140.67,"That was the trade that he knew."],[2142.03,"He said. So I supported myself."],[2144.05,"And he said the important part of that is not just that you aren't a burden to other people, but that you're able to help other people."],[2150.93,"'re able to. You help other people"],[2155.63,"And so this is this is um part of, and we'll see more of this in his epistles, but this is St."],[2163.79,"Paul's understanding of why there are wealthy Christians."],[2176.83,"That sounds very negative towards rich people."],[2181.63,"But so for St."],[2183.71,"Paul, if you have some wealth, if you have some money, if you've earned some money, that's a blessing."],[2190.67,"Not a blessing in the sense that, wow, you've got some money, so now you can go have fun and live a great lifestyle."],[2196.05,"But that's a blessing in that now you can use that to help people who are in need."],[2201.97,"And doing that is the real blessing."],[2204.29,"And so he quotes this saying of Christ, which is interesting because it occurs nowhere in the Gospels."],[2211.57,"So this saying of Jesus that St."],[2213.89,"Paul quotes here is something that Jesus said that had circulated orally in the Christian community."],[2224.21,"Yeah, obviously, unless I have the document as well."],[2226.77,"I always assumed it."],[2228.21,"And he says, remember the words, meaning that this isn't the first time they've heard it."],[2232.13,"So this is something that was well known."],[2235.5,"It is more blessed to give than to receive."],[2238.11,"So we see somebody who's wealthy and we say, Wow, he's really been blessed."],[2242.03,"It's like, no, we should see somebody giving and say, He's really been blessed."],[2247.31,"That's the greater blessing is the person who gives."],[2253.79,"And when he had said these things, he knelt down and prayed with them all."],[2258.35,"Then they all wept freely and fell on Paul's neck and kissed him, sorrowing most of all for the words which he spoke, that they would see his face no more."],[2267.31,"And they accompanied him to the ship."],[2270.51,"So this is their response."],[2272.35,"They're sad to see Paul go."],[2274.03,"They're very sad that they're not going to see him again, uh, if that's correct."],[2278.35,"That St. Paul has told him."],[2280.43,"Um, but so this this passage here in at the second half of Acts chapter 20 is very famous."],[2287.43,"Because it's a place where we not only see St."],[2290.95,"Paul's pastoral heart, we talked about this a little bit."],[2293.91,"Saint Paul is staying in these places for years."],[2297.77,"We tend to think of the saints, you know, like St."],[2300.25,"Paul traveled, he preached these powerful sermons, you know, and he preached the gospel and he suffered these things."],[2305.05,"You know, sort of boiled down his life."],[2306.73,"He spent three years in Ephesus just getting to know these people."],[2310.49,"He was baptizing them and baptizing their children and celebrating the Eucharist and coming and praying with them and blessing them when they were sick, and you know, watching them have kids and get married. and right"],[2324.47,"That that's a big part of who St."],[2326.63,"Paul was. And we see that reflected here as he speaks to them."],[2330.49,"And we also see how how Saint Paul, because he's talking to the presbyters he's appointed to now govern the church in Ephesus."],[2338.73,"We see how Saint Paul sees leadership."],[2342.98,"In the church and for Christians outside the church, how he understands a leader works, which is very different than how you know we typically understand."],[2351.62,"You know, the leader's the boss, the leader's in charge, leader's one who tells other people what to do."],[2357.16,"And so it's sort of a practical playing out."],[2359.24,"Remember, Christ said that."],[2360.86,"He said that the lead the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them."],[2364.56,"It should not be with you."],[2365.68,"The one of you who wants to be great should be a servant."],[2368.0,"Here's St. Paul is showing us what that looks like. for somebody to be a leader and be a servant, you know, at the same time"],[2377.72,"Paul just didn't preach, he loved on them."],[2379.86,"He actually did, he actually did it."],[2382.5,"He didn't just tell them."],[2384.27,"But he did it."],[2385.07,"Yeah. They could know for sure that Christ loved them because St."],[2390.51,"Paul loved them."],[2394.99,"You know? So yeah, that's he he he he uh didn't just hear the word of God, he did it."],[2403.95,"Yeah, it would not be convincing that God loves you if the person who told you that treated you like turd."],[2413.01,"If he treated them the same way, you know, a lot of these were slaves, if he treated them the way their Roman masters treated them."],[2421.69,"It wouldn't matter how revolutionary what he was saying was."],[2424.71,"It'd be the same old stuff."],[2426.79,"And a lot of them were women."],[2428.15,"If he treated them the way their husbands treated them."],[2433.19,"No matter how revolutionary what he was saying was."],[2435.93,"No, God loves men and women alike, you know, but I'm still gonna treat you like a second class human being."],[2444.79,"It wouldn't go anywhere."],[2446.71,"You know, and so he he had to, and that that is, I think the biggest thing, more than his rabbinical training and more than any rhetorical skill, although he had both."],[2457.59,"I think that's what made his preaching so effective in these places was that he actually lived it out"],[2465.15,"In the way that a lot of the other leaders, including a lot of the leaders in synagogues and that kind of thing, did."],[2471.87,"You know, and they could see the difference."],[2487.39,"Yeah. Took a paycheck and left."],[2491.55,"Yeah. Yeah. So it's and it's it's again it's related to, you know, even even though today, at least at this moment, and uh as any Russian who was alive in 1918 could tell you, it can turn around very quickly."],[2508.71,"But uh at this moment we don't face persecution."],[2512.47,"You know, it's very unlikely that anyone in this room or listening to this on the internet is going to be tortured to death for being a Christian."],[2520.07,"Not totally impossible, but unlikely, at least at this present moment."],[2525.91,"Um but in the same way that we were talking about how the Roman world saw Christians willing to suffer and die for their faith, and that transformed them."],[2537.63,"These people in Ephesus see how St."],[2540.11,"Paul lives his life, even when he's not being persecuted."],[2544.57,"And they see that it's different."],[2545.85,"different This is than everyone else."],[2546.33,"And that goes back to, remember, that was the whole point of Israel"],[2553.47,"Israel was to be a light to the nations."],[2555.39,"They were supposed to live in a fundamentally different way."],[2558.83,"Live a life that was holy and pure and good, and then the other nations would see them and want to become like them."],[2564.67,"And they sort of failed at that."],[2566.67,"But that's the charge that Christ gave to us as Christians."],[2571.23,"You're the light of the world."],[2573.39,"You're the salt of the earth."],[2575.79,"Salt loses its saltiness, that's it."],[2580.03,"So we have that ability, even in a country like this where we don't face persecution, to live our lives following Christ in a way that's different from the world around us."],[2591.31,"And if we do that, that is the most effective thing we can do"],[2597.27,"More effective than any words that come out of our mouth in terms of showing people, hey, there's something actually here."],[2605.11,"That's not like the new diet plan or exercise plan, or right?"],[2610.31,"These people actually have something that's real."],[2613.75,"And I should go and go and investigate that."],[2618.31,"So this is a good place to stop since we're at the end of a chapter."],[2621.75,"So next week we'll get into chapter 21."],[2625.51,"Thank you, everybody."],[2626.95,"Thank you. Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2636.23,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com"],[2641.95,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.52,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:5-6 - Sailing from Philippi to Troas","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Notice again \"<b>we</b>\" - <b>St Luke</b> is there too</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:6</b>: sailed from <b>Philippi</b> after the <b>days of unleavened bread</b>, five days to <b>Troas</b>, stayed <b>seven days</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Went up north, around, then down toward Antioch - <b>longer, circuitous route</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Is Troas the same as <b>Troy</b>? <b>No</b></li><li class=\"d1\">may have claimed to be at some point</li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>Roman Troy</b> not in the same spot as the Troy of the <b>Trojan War</b></li><li class=\"d1\">several places claimed it; by this point they'd <b>lost track</b> of where it was</li></ul>"},{"t":83.48,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:7 - First day of the week, breaking bread","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"On the <b>first day of the week</b>, when the disciples came together to <b>break bread</b>\" - pausing</li><li class=\"d0\">He's been saying all along: Christians still go to the <b>synagogue</b>, preaching and learning Christ there on the <b>Sabbath</b>, seventh day</li><li class=\"d1\">now \"here in <b>black and white</b>\": <b>first day</b> - <b>just the Christians</b> gathering</li><li class=\"d1\">on <b>Sunday</b>, to <b>break bread</b> = celebrating the <b>Eucharist</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Different from what they do on Saturday in the synagogue</li></ul>"},{"t":134.31,"lv":3,"h":"Two pieces of our liturgy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Where we get the <b>two parts of our liturgy</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>First part</b>: sing <b>Psalms</b>, read <b>Scripture</b>, <b>preach</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= what they did in the <b>synagogue on the Sabbath</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Second part</b>: celebrate the <b>Eucharist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= what they did on <b>Sunday</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Second century</b>: Christians thrown out of the synagogue</li><li class=\"d1\">took the synagogue part and moved it to Sunday too</li><li class=\"d1\">whole thing on Sunday as a <b>Christian gathering</b></li></ul>"},{"t":173.02,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:7-9 - Paul preaches till midnight","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:7</b>: Paul, ready to depart next day, spoke and <b>continued his message until midnight</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"I don't think I could get away with a half hour\" - people leaving, asleep, <b>rolling eyes</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why: he's about to leave - \"whatever I've got to say, I need to say it <b>now</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: three months' worth of scrolls gathered together</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:9</b>: in a window sat a young man named <b>Eutychus</b>, sinking into deep sleep</li><li class=\"d1\">Greek word = very young, \"probably a <b>teenager</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Windows had <b>no glass</b> - a <b>hole in the wall</b></li><li class=\"d1\">upper rooms, <b>second floor</b>; sitting in the frame, probably wanted <b>fresh air</b>, dozing off</li></ul>"},{"t":276.47,"lv":3,"h":"Lamps and the seven-branch lampstand","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Many lamps</b> in the upper room\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Do our candles symbolize bringing our lamps? Related</li><li class=\"d1\">Christian gathering places for the first day had <b>seven-branch lampstands</b>, like the <b>temple's</b></li><li class=\"d1\">explicit in <b>Revelation</b> when we get there</li><li class=\"d0\">Another <b>temple worship / altar</b> connection</li><li class=\"d0\">One in the <b>tabernacle</b>, one in the <b>temple</b>, one in <b>our altar</b></li><li class=\"d1\">already being done then</li></ul>"},{"t":351.08,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:9-12 - Eutychus falls and is raised","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:9</b>: overcome by sleep, as Paul kept speaking, <b>fell from the third story</b>, taken up <b>dead</b></li><li class=\"d1\">falls about <b>25 feet</b>, lands on the road, dead</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:10</b>: Paul went down, <b>fell on him</b>, embraced him: \"<b>Do not trouble yourselves, for his life is in him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= \"don't panic\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:11-12</b>: Paul came up, <b>broke bread</b>, ate, talked till <b>daybreak</b>, departed</li><li class=\"d1\">they brought the young man in <b>alive</b>, \"not a little comforted\" - \"underplayed quasi-British translation\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He <b>eats</b> → they know he's alive</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paul raised him from the dead</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>Luke lists the people</b> there: witnesses from different cities - \"I remember when that happened\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Breaking of bread comes <b>after the sermon</b></li><li class=\"d1\">couldn't \"receive the Eucharist and <b>bail out</b>\" before a sermon past midnight</li></ul>"},{"t":461.11,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:13-16 - Voyage to Miletus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Again \"<b>we</b>\" - Luke still there</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:13</b>: went ahead to the ship, sailed to <b>Assos</b>, intending to take Paul aboard</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul going <b>on foot</b> for part - <b>Roman road</b> ran down the coast</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:14-15</b>: <b>Mitylene</b>, opposite <b>Chios</b>, <b>Samos</b>, <b>Trogyllium</b>, then <b>Miletus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"our <b>travel log</b> of the coast of Asia Minor in the Roman period\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:16</b>: Paul decided to <b>sail past Ephesus</b> to avoid spending time in Asia - hurrying to <b>Jerusalem for Pentecost</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Gives the length of the third journey</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>year and a half at Ephesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">last time trying to reach Jerusalem for <b>Passover</b>; now <b>Pentecost</b>, 50 days later</li><li class=\"d1\">over <b>two years</b> by the end</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Let's not stop at Ephesus\" - that's the plan, at least</li></ul>"},{"t":575.2,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:17-21 - Elders at Miletus; nothing held back","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:17</b>: from Miletus sends to Ephesus, calls the <b>elders (presbyters)</b> he appointed</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't want to stop at Ephesus but wants to see them → \"come up and visit\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:18-20</b>: \"you know <b>how I lived</b> among you\", serving the Lord with <b>humility, tears, trials</b> - plotting of the Jews</li><li class=\"d1\">kept back <b>nothing</b> helpful, taught <b>publicly and house to house</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Telling the leaders: <b>this is what you continue to do</b> when I'm not there</li><li class=\"d0\">Taught <b>for free</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not normal then or now - you pay <b>tuition</b></li><li class=\"d1\">study with a philosopher: pay directly; with a craftsman: pay with <b>labor</b>, grunt work</li><li class=\"d1\">\"didn't say buy my book for $19.99\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Do it <b>publicly</b>, house to house, first-day gathering, synagogue, <b>marketplaces</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to <b>Jews and Greeks</b> - everybody</li><li class=\"d0\">Not looking to <b>get rich</b> off the kingdom</li></ul>"},{"t":712.38,"lv":3,"h":"Q: secret doctrines","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Is this against <b>secret doctrines</b> kept back from most?</li><li class=\"d1\">yes - \"that's the <b>publicly</b> part\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Said it all <b>in the open</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Proclaim it to everybody - that's what you need to do too\"</li></ul>"},{"t":768.1,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:21 - Repentance and faith; the Shema","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Preached <b>repentance toward God</b> and <b>faith toward our Lord Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Some say Paul doesn't believe in the <b>Trinity</b> - \"God and Jesus\" too separate</li><li class=\"d1\">not true: he says \"<b>our Lord</b> Jesus Christ\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><i>Kyrios</i> = another title for the <b>God of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Shema</b> (Deuteronomy): \"Hear, O Israel, the <b>Lord</b> your <b>God</b>, the <b>Lord</b> is one\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Lord and God are <b>one</b> there</li><li class=\"d0\">So \"God and our Lord Jesus Christ\" = Father and Christ <b>one</b> → Trinitarian, \"or at least binitarian\" statement</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Corinthians</b>: Paul inserts the names <b>Jesus and the Father</b> into the words of the Shema in Greek</li><li class=\"d1\">makes clear the one God of Israel is <b>three persons</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Any listener would catch it - heard the Shema at synagogue <b>every meeting</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Pharisees</b> used it like Orthodox use the <b>Jesus Prayer</b>, recited again and again</li></ul>"},{"t":920.17,"lv":3,"h":"Faith is not a true-false test","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two things: <b>repentance and faith</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Faith is <b>not passing a true-false test</b></li><li class=\"d1\">one God: true; three persons: true; Jesus died for my sin: true - mark all true, \"you have faith\"</li><li class=\"d1\">thinking of faith as against <b>modern atheists</b>: not what the Bible means</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>James</b> will make it clear: <b>every demon in hell</b> gets the test right</li><li class=\"d1\">Satan knows one God, three persons, that Jesus died for the world's sins - \"he <b>knows</b> it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not doing him any good\" - we wouldn't say he has faith</li><li class=\"d0\">Word includes <b>faithfulness</b>: <b>loyalty, allegiance</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>No atheists</b> when the NT was written - nobody thought there were no gods</li><li class=\"d1\">so it's not \"which God\": faith in Jesus = <b>loyal to him</b> as opposed to other gods, lords, masters</li><li class=\"d1\">you <b>worship him</b>, give him glory</li></ul>"},{"t":1067.37,"lv":3,"h":"Why this matters for Romans","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Next book will be <b>Romans</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Saved by faith\" read as the true-false test → won't understand Paul - \"you're going to become a <b>Lutheran</b>\" (not kidding)</li><li class=\"d1\">the problem <b>James</b> points to: \"just saved by believing, doesn't matter what you do\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Real faith means <b>doing a whole bunch of things</b> and <b>not doing</b> others</li><li class=\"d0\">Here Paul isn't saying repent once, profess Messiah once, \"boom, you're saved\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ongoing</b>: they must continue to preach <b>repentance toward God</b> and <b>faith in Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people need to continue in both</li></ul>"},{"t":1158.59,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:22-24 - Bound in the Spirit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:22-23</b>: \"I go <b>bound in the Spirit</b> to Jerusalem\", not knowing what will happen, except the Holy Spirit testifies in every city that <b>chains and tribulations</b> await</li><li class=\"d0\">Firm impression bad things will happen</li><li class=\"d1\">reasons beyond the Spirit: <b>persecution</b> in Jerusalem last time in Acts</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Peter</b> in prison, <b>James son of Zebedee</b> killed, <b>Stephen</b> killed</li><li class=\"d1\">run-ins with <b>synagogue communities</b> on the way; word reached Jewish leaders</li><li class=\"d0\">May be <b>killed</b> → why the <b>charge to Ephesus's leadership</b> matters, in case they never see him again \"in the body\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:24</b>: \"none of these things move me\", not counting life dear, to <b>finish my race with joy</b> and the ministry to testify to the <b>gospel of the grace of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"maybe I won't go\" - he's <b>still going</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"if this is the time I'm going to die, then so be it\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1274.58,"lv":3,"h":"Q: why is he so determined to go to Jerusalem?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Is the feast the motivation? Several things</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Collection</b> from the new <b>Gentile churches</b> for the Christians in Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d1\">Judean <b>peasants</b> in crushing poverty</li><li class=\"d1\">Christians now <b>pariahs</b> in the Jewish community on top - \"other peasants don't even like them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He needs to <b>deliver</b> it, there for the feast</li><li class=\"d0\">Believes he must go \"as much as he knows this is not going to be pleasant\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1333.33,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:25-27 - Innocent of the blood of all men","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:25</b>: \"you...will see my face <b>no more</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">convinced he won't be seen again <b>in the body</b></li><li class=\"d1\">spent <b>a year and a half</b> in Ephesus preaching, appointing presbyters, working with them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:26</b>: \"I am <b>innocent of the blood of all men</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">interesting: who thought he wasn't? Someone who read early Acts - <b>persecuting Christians</b>, <b>Stephen</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:27</b>: \"not shunned to declare to you the <b>whole counsel of God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">why innocent? <b>because of what he's preached</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not why he's innocent of the earlier blood</li></ul>"},{"t":1415.92,"lv":3,"h":"Repentance is real: 1 Kings and Corinth","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Parallel in <b>1 Kings</b> - <b>Solomon</b> \"royally messed up\"</li><li class=\"d1\">we think of him as great; he was \"really <b>wicked</b>\" → loses the kingdom, divided</li><li class=\"d1\">son gets <b>two tribes</b>; ten go to <b>Jeroboam son of Nebat</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Prophet tells Jeroboam: I'll make your throne <b>eternal</b> like <b>David's</b> if you walk in my ways \"<b>like David did</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">aside from the <b>adultery and murder</b> - but shows <b>repentance is real</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul repented and was <b>baptized</b> → no longer a murderer</li><li class=\"d1\">epistles: \"I <b>was</b> a murderer\" - <b>past tense</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Corinthians</b> list: theft, drunkenness, homosexuality, adultery… \"<b>and such were some of you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"but you were <b>washed</b>\" - done</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just imagery: baptized <b>die and rise</b> to new life</li><li class=\"d1\">fathers: <b>tears of repentance</b> like a <b>second baptism</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"we are a different person after that\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So the innocence isn't about before - <b>baptism took care of that</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1627.93,"lv":3,"h":"Silence makes us accessory","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Innocent because he preached <b>everything publicly to everyone</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Reverse: someone in sin, <b>perishing</b>, needing to hear Christ's love, and we <b>don't tell them or help</b>, \"we don't care\"</li><li class=\"d1\">we're <b>guilty, an accessory</b> in modern legal terms</li></ul>"},{"t":1662.22,"lv":3,"h":"Q: the neighbors on drugs","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: neighbors next door are <b>drug heads</b>, some <b>violent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bought a <b>St Michael candle</b> for Stephan, said \"I'll pray for you\"; scared of them</li><li class=\"d0\">Answer: that's not refusing to speak - <b>praying and reaching out</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul is talking to the <b>presbyters</b>, future church leaders</li><li class=\"d1\">can't <b>shrink away</b> or get scared of people in the church</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I don't want to make waves\", \"he gives a lot of money\" → <b>accessory</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Can't <b>force</b> anyone</li><li class=\"d1\">but a difference from <b>withholding what you know they need to hear</b>, \"chickening out\"</li><li class=\"d0\">If they go down that road, they may <b>destroy themselves</b> → too late to say something</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: innocent because he laid it out <b>all the time</b> - \"you need to do the same\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Where I stole the title of my podcast, my blog\" - the <b>whole counsel of God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1793.4,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:28 - Take heed; the church bought with his own blood","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:28</b>: \"take heed to yourselves and to all the flock...the Holy Spirit has made you <b>overseers</b> to shepherd the church of God which he <b>purchased with his own blood</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Important: \"<b>God has blood</b>\" - the <b>incarnation</b> right there</li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus Christ is God and has blood</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Take heed to yourselves</b> first - your own life in order - then those under your authority</li><li class=\"d1\">not just presbyters or priests - <b>all of us</b>: boss, parent, aunt, uncle, grandparent</li><li class=\"d0\">Each is so precious to God that he <b>died</b> for them, \"purchased at a very high price\"</li><li class=\"d1\">remember who they are → informs how you <b>treat, care for, guide, lead</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1914.87,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:29-31 - Wolves and tears","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:29-30</b>: people will come to <b>lead them off</b>, harm them - \"<b>savage wolves</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">also \"from among yourselves men will rise up speaking <b>perverse things</b>\" to draw disciples after themselves</li><li class=\"d1\">not just outsiders - family, community members become <b>like wolves</b> and turn on each other</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:31</b>: \"<b>three years</b> I did not cease to warn everyone <b>night and day with tears</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"I'm nowhere near as good a pastor as St Paul - I'm working on it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"my job, my duty\"; <b>passionately cares</b> about each one</li><li class=\"d0\">When they go astray: response not <b>anger</b>, not <b>excommunication</b> - <b>tears</b></li><li class=\"d1\">treats what happens to them as if it <b>happened to himself</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2017.66,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:32 - The word of his grace and the inheritance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:32</b>: \"I commend you to <b>God and to the word of his grace</b>, able to <b>build you up</b> and give you an <b>inheritance</b> among all those sanctified\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He won't be able to give more sermons</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Word of his grace\" here = the <b>Scriptures</b></li><li class=\"d1\">continue in it → <b>learn and grow</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Inheritance</b> isn't \"somebody left me something in a will\"</li><li class=\"d1\">OT: the <b>Promised Land</b>; each tribe, family had an inheritance in it</li><li class=\"d1\">so = the <b>world to come</b>, <b>glory with God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2095.26,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:33-35 - More blessed to give","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:33-34</b>: \"I have coveted <b>no one's silver or gold</b>\"; these <b>hands</b> provided for my needs - labored as a <b>tentmaker</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"no buy my book, no buy me a house\" - not here to make money</li><li class=\"d1\">→ you're not here to <b>enrich yourselves</b> either</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:35</b>: \"support the weak\"; remember <b>Jesus</b>: \"it is more blessed to give than to receive\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the point: not just not a <b>burden</b>, but able to <b>help others</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's understanding of <b>why there are wealthy Christians</b> - more in the epistles</li><li class=\"d1\">wealth is a blessing so you can <b>help people in need</b> - \"doing that is the real blessing\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Saying of Christ occurs <b>nowhere in the Gospels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">circulated <b>orally</b> in the Christian community</li><li class=\"d1\">\"remember the words\" → well known to them</li><li class=\"d0\">We see the wealthy and say \"blessed\"; instead see <b>the giver</b> - \"the greater blessing\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2253.79,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 20:36-38 - Farewell on the shore","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:36</b>: knelt and <b>prayed</b> with them all</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>20:37-38</b>: wept freely, fell on his neck, <b>kissed him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sorrowing most that they'd <b>see his face no more</b></li><li class=\"d1\">accompanied him to the ship</li><li class=\"d0\">Sad to see him go - if Paul is correct</li></ul>"},{"t":2280.43,"lv":2,"h":"Paul's pastoral heart and leadership as service","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Second half of Acts 20 is <b>very famous</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Shows Paul's <b>pastoral heart</b>: he stays places for <b>years</b></li><li class=\"d1\">we boil the saints down to traveling, powerful sermons, suffering</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>three years in Ephesus</b> getting to know people: <b>baptizing</b> them and their children, <b>Eucharist</b>, praying, <b>blessing the sick</b>, watching them marry and have kids</li><li class=\"d0\">Also how Paul sees <b>leadership</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"the boss, in charge, tells people what to do\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ: <b>rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them</b>; \"should not be so with you\"; whoever wants to be great must be a <b>servant</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul shows what a <b>leader and servant</b> looks like</li></ul>"},{"t":2377.72,"lv":3,"h":"Love made the preaching credible","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul didn't just preach, he <b>loved on them</b> - \"he actually did it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they could know <b>Christ loved them</b> because Paul loved them</li><li class=\"d0\">Not convincing that God loves you if the messenger treated you \"like <b>turd</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">many were <b>slaves</b>: if he treated them as their <b>Roman masters</b> did → \"same old stuff\"</li><li class=\"d1\">many were <b>women</b>: treating them as their husbands did → \"second-class human being\" - \"wouldn't go anywhere\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Biggest thing, \"more than his <b>rabbinical training</b> and <b>rhetorical skill</b>\": he <b>lived it out</b></li><li class=\"d1\">unlike many other leaders, incl. synagogue leaders - \"<b>took a paycheck and left</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they could see the difference\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2491.55,"lv":2,"h":"Living differently, even without persecution","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Today we don't face <b>persecution</b> - very unlikely anyone here will be <b>tortured to death</b> for being Christian</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not totally impossible\" - as any Russian alive in <b>1918</b> could say, it can turn around fast</li><li class=\"d0\">As Roman world saw Christians <b>suffer and die</b> and was transformed</li><li class=\"d1\">Ephesians saw how Paul <b>lived</b>, even <b>not</b> persecuted - \"different from everyone else\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Goes back to <b>Israel</b>: to be a <b>light to the nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">live <b>holy, pure, good</b>, others want to become like them - \"sort of failed at that\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ's charge to us: <b>light of the world</b>, <b>salt of the earth</b> - \"salt loses its saltiness, that's it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Even here we can live <b>following Christ differently</b> from the world</li><li class=\"d1\">\"most effective thing we can do\", <b>more than any words</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people see \"there's something actually here\" - not like a <b>new diet or exercise plan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I should go and investigate that\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>Acts 21</b>"});
